      },
      "message": "feat(post): probing hooks for the Haas, Mazak and Siemens posts\n\nVoice onProbeMove / onProbeRetreat / onProbeResult in haas.cps (G31,\n#5061-#5063, #3000/#3006, G10 L2), mazak.cps (G31 + macro, IF..GOTO with\nunique labels, M00 operator stop) and sinumerik.cps (MEAS=1, $AC_MEA,\n$AA_MW, SETAL, $P_UIFR settable frames; G58/G59 refused by name), each\nfrom its dialect's public programming documentation. The three posts\nno longer start a spindle at 0 rpm (a touch probe states none).\nheidenhain.cps keeps the engine's named refusal: its ISO manual states\nno skip move or trip-position variable, and no Q parameter is guessed.\n\nPinned by crates/app/tests/probe_dialects.rs with bore-centre goldens\nunder golden/nc/{haas,mazak,sinumerik}/ and the Heidenhain refusal.\n\nFixes #173\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
