      "message": "fix(post): probe deviations fold their sign in the Haas, Mazak and Sinumerik posts\n\nonProbeResult wrote each deviation as mean - expected with the expected\nvalue printed signed, so an edge or outside-corner probe (negative\nexpected value) posted a doubled sign: #190=#100--2 / R90=R50--2. The\nsign is now folded into the operator (mean + |expected|), as the Tormach\npost already does. The right-hand side is left unbracketed: the fold\nalone fixes the defect and the bore-centre goldens stay byte-identical.\n\nPinned by haas_/mazak_/sinumerik_edge_deviation_folds_its_sign in\nprobe_dialects (no '--', '+-' or '-+' anywhere; folded deviation line).\n\nRefs #173\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
