        "date": "2026-11-10T03:39:56Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): probing on an inverted X/Y axis for the Haas post\n\nhaas.cps declares probeAxisInversion = true: the engine's mirror (#465)\nnegates the touch target and trip, back-off delta and found expected\nvalues, and the Haas probing hooks (#173) post that stream unchanged -\nG31 / #5061.. / G10 L2 P / #5221.. all read in the controller's frame,\nso the written work offset is the physical correction.\n\ninverted_probe runs every case for Fanuc and Haas (face, edge, corners,\nbore, boss on standard / inverted X / Y / XY machines), plus a new\nbyte-identity test that the flag changes nothing on a standard machine.\nThe refusal is pinned on a shipped script with its flag line removed.\n\nFixes #392\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
